.SH NAME
md__2home_2umar_2Desktop_2WorkShop_2GLL_2Ftp-FM_2README \- README 
.PP
 
.br
.PP
Serve as a fast local http server and FTP utility\&. 
.br
 You can also use it to browse files like File Manager but in the Navigator\&.
.PP
Quite simple to use\&. Type the \fC--help\fP flag to get the usage summary\&.
.PP
NOTE: By default, if the target directory contains an \fC\&.html\fP or \fC\&.htm\fP index, priority is given to displaying these files\&.
.SS "Project Structure"
.SS "base Structure"
config / - basic configuration, include/ - header files src / - source files
.SS "After build"
.IP "\(bu" 2
bin/ - hold the final binary
.IP "\(bu" 2
lib/ - hold the needed library
.PP
.SS "Prelude"
.PP
.nf
$ git clone https://github\&.com/Galsen\-Low\-Level/Ftp\-FM \-\-recursive 
.fi
.PP
.SS "Quick assessment"
This section is for those who want to get a quick overview of the project using Docker\&. Here's an example:
.PP
.PP
.nf
                        ___________
                        v          v
$ docker  run   \-v ~/Desktop/:/opt/local \-p 9090:9090 ftpfm   /ftp\-FM/bin/ftpFM  \-t /opt/local
                                   ^\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-^
.fi
.PP
 \fIThe contents of the Desktop folder are volume-mounted on /opt/local and the program will point to this folder to display the contents of the volume-mounted folder\&.\fP
.SS "### Build"
The default build tool is \fCCmake\fP
.PP
to build it, use the following command
.PP
.PP
.nf
cmake \-B build 
cmake \-\-build build  
.fi
.PP
.PP
the binary source is located in the \&./bin folder the \&./lib folder contains the libraries (you can browse them) 
.br
.SS "Have fun"
launch binary :
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ \&./bin/ftpfm \-h # to get help 
$ \&./bin/ftpfm  # launch on default port 9090 
.fi
.PP
